  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smart farming, healthy food</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will contribute to the development of sustainable and climate resilient smallholder vegetable-based cropping systems in the Barisal and Chittagong Divisions.This includes the promotion of climate-resilient and sustainable production practices, the improvement of access to input and output markets for smallholder farmers, and the operationalization of a climate smart Bangladesh GAP curriculum.This will, among other things, result in:&#x2022;	25,000 smallholder farmers (8,750 male and 16,250 female) with increased productivity and income; and&#x2022;	10,000 farmers selling safe vegetables into premium markets via rural collection and marketing centers.</narrative>
  </description>
